# LOOM-8 demo: hyperpop, 160 BPM, A minor (F G Am Em). (tools/demos/render.sh renders it; its bank is
# build/demos/hyperpop.bin: a bar sung high and tuned hard, and an 808, both made by tools/demos/make_banks.py.)
#   T1 kit: kick, clap and snare, metallic hats with rolls (multiply), the fm drum as a metallic hit, the
#      kit's bus compressed and driven hard
#   T2 sample: the 808 (user 2, its root C2), mono, gliding (portamento trick), driven
#   T3 brocade "sequin", seven saws spread wide: the supersaw chords, ducked by the kick (the pump LFO)
#   T4 slice: the voice in 16, crushed, chopped with octave and fifth locks
#   T5 gingham "picnic", the circuit-bent toy, through the arp (1/16, up, two octaves, latched): the chord held by
#      hand each bar
#   T6 rayon "glass bell": sparkles in the intro and the break
#   T7 voile "sheer lead": a sung topline gliding over drop 2
# Song: intro 4, build 4 (snare build), drop 8, break 4 (the voice and the 808 alone, throws), build 2, drop 2 8
# (the arp and the topline in), outro 4 (the voice echoing).
master 4096
samples build/demos/hyperpop.bin
bpm 160

# ---- the sounds (hyperpop: the brightest of the six. Hard, clipped drums on top, hats loud, a sub that is all
# 808, the chords thin and up high, the voice pitched up and crushed; short bright rooms, a master pushed loud)
# T1 the kit: a deep kick with a big pitch drop, driven (the key's own drive), a snappy snare and a bright clap
# layered, hats metallic and high (the shimmer, not the band), the bus compressed and driven; the fm drum (key
# 11) tuned high and short, with a lot of modulation: the metallic "latex" hit
knob 1 d1.k1 66
knob 1 d1.k2 58
knob 1 d1.k3 120
knob 1 d1.k4 96
knob 1 d1.drive 60
knob 1 d2.k1 96
knob 1 d2.k2 30
knob 1 d2.k3 110
knob 1 d2.volume 74
knob 1 d5.k1 118
knob 1 d5.k2 50
knob 1 d5.volume 86
knob 1 d3.k1 112
knob 1 d3.k3 100
knob 1 d3.k4 30
knob 1 d3.volume 86
knob 1 d4.k1 112
knob 1 d4.k3 100
knob 1 d4.k4 30
knob 1 d4.k2 70
knob 1 d4.volume 80
knob 1 d11.k1 118
knob 1 d11.k2 30
knob 1 d11.k3 110
knob 1 d11.k4 60
knob 1 d11.volume 70
knob 1 ftype dynamic
knob 1 cut 10
knob 1 res 80
knob 1 fenv 76
knob 1 level 95
knob 1 send2 8
# T2 the 808 (user 2, its root C2): mono, gliding, driven bright enough to read on a small speaker
knob 2 engine sample
knob 2 e1 u2
knob 2 e4 one-shot
knob 2 vmode mono
knob 2 porta 40
knob 2 a 0
knob 2 d 100
knob 2 s 127
knob 2 r 40
knob 2 cut 110
knob 2 ktrk 0
knob 2 ctype drive
knob 2 camt 96
knob 2 ctone 116
knob 2 cmix 127
knob 2 brain no
knob 2 level 97
# T3 brocade "sequin": seven saws spread wide, played high, through its own drive, pumped by the kick
preset 3 sequin brocade
knob 3 e2 70
knob 3 e4 127
knob 3 s 70
knob 3 r 56
knob 3 cut 100
knob 3 res 20
knob 3 ltype pump
knob 3 lspeed track_1
knob 3 lamt 100
knob 3 brain no
knob 3 level 82
knob 3 send1 20
knob 3 send2 22
# T4 the voice in 16 slices, mono: bitcrushed (bits more than rate: bright grit), into the delay
knob 4 engine slice
preset 4 chop slice
knob 4 e1 u1
knob 4 e4 127
knob 4 vmode mono
knob 4 cut 127
knob 4 ctype crush
knob 4 camt 46
knob 4 ctone 96
knob 4 cmix 80
knob 4 brain no
knob 4 level 95
knob 4 send1 34
knob 4 send2 22
# T5 gingham "picnic", the circuit-bent toy, through the arp
preset 5 picnic gingham
knob 5 brain no
knob 5 player arp
knob 5 p1 1/16
knob 5 p2 up
knob 5 p3 2
knob 5 p4 1
knob 5 ap1 short
knob 5 ap4 wide
knob 5 level 97
knob 5 send1 40
# T6 rayon "glass bell": sparkles
preset 6 glass_bell rayon
knob 6 brain no
knob 6 level 84
knob 6 send1 50
knob 6 send2 40
# T7 voile "sheer lead": the sung topline, bright
preset 7 sheer_lead voile
knob 7 brain no
knob 7 e2 95
knob 7 e3 115
knob 7 cut 120
knob 7 level 89
knob 7 send1 36
knob 7 send2 26
# FX I a bright eighth-note ping-pong; FX II a small bright plate (short, open on top)
knob 11 engine delay
knob 11 e1 72
knob 11 e3 54
knob 11 e4 96
knob 12 engine plate
knob 12 e1 70
knob 12 e3 64
knob 12 e4 40
# the master: the top lifted (the genre wants it sharp), the bottom firm,
# the bus compressor hard and the level up: the limiter at work, as these records are
mst hi 96
mst lo 72
mst mid 54
mst comp 60
mst level 96

# ---- T1 the kit: kick 1, snare 2, hat 3, open 4, clap 5
